    }
  },
  "AND": {
    "left": {
      "raw_text": "Patients on Sandostatin Lar (long acting somatostatin analogue) must be on a stable dose for 30 days prior to study entry and short acting somatostatin analogues must be judged to be on a clinically stable dose by the investigator prior to study entry"
    }
  },
  "AND": {
    "left": {
      "raw_text": "Must have a life expectancy of greater than three (3) months"
    }
  },
  "AND": {
    "left": {
      "raw_text": "Karnofsky Performance Status > 60"
    }
  },
  "AND": {
    "left": {
      "OR": {
        "left": {
          "raw_text": "Female patients must have a negative serum pregnancy test at screening. (Not applicable to patients with bilateral oophorectomy and/or hysterectomy or to those patients who are postmenopausal.)"
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Entities:

* Patients
* Biopsy-proven metastatic carcinoid tumors
* Other neuroendocrine tumors
* Islet cell
* Gastrinomas
* VIPomas
* Sandostatin Lar
* Long acting somatostatin analogue
* Short acting somatostatin analogues
* Karnofsky Performance Status
* Serum pregnancy test
* Bilateral oophorectomy
* Hysterectomy
* Postmenopausal

Relations:

* Patients have biopsy-proven metastatic carcinoid tumors or other neuroendocrine tumors
* Patients have at least one measurable lesion (other than bone)
* Patients have no major impairment of renal or hepatic function
* Patients on Sandostatin Lar must be on a stable dose for 30 days prior to study entry
* Patients must have a life expectancy of greater than three (3) months
* Patients must have a Karnofsky Performance Status > 60
* Female patients must have a negative serum pregnancy test at screening 

